      "v": 1,
      "zh": "约瑟被带下埃及去。有一个埃及人，是法老的内臣―护卫长波提乏，从那些带下他来的以实玛利人手下买了他去。",
      "en": "Now Joseph had been brought down to Egypt.[NOTE:1] An Egyptian named Potiphar, an official of Pharaoh and the captain of the guard,[NOTE:2] purchased him from[NOTE:3] the Ishmaelites who had brought him there.",
      "notes": [
        "The disjunctive clause resumes the earlier narrative pertaining to Joseph by recapitulating the event described in 37:36. The perfect verbal form is given a past perfect translation to restore the sequence of the narrative for the reader.",
        "Captain of the guard. See the note on this phrase in Gen 37:36.",
        "Heb “from the hand of.”"
      ],
