    {
      "v": 7,
      "zh": "这事以后，约瑟主人的妻以目送情给约瑟，说：「你与我同寝吧！」",
      "en": "Soon after these things, his master’s wife took notice of[NOTE:1] Joseph and said, “Come to bed with me.”[NOTE:2]",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “she lifted up her eyes toward,” an expression that emphasizes her deliberate and careful scrutiny of him.",
        "The story of Joseph and Potiphar’s wife has long been connected with the wisdom warnings about the strange woman who tries to seduce the young man with her boldness and directness (see Prov 5-7, especially 7:6-27). This is part of the literary background of the story of Joseph that gives it a wisdom flavor. See G. von Rad, God at Work in Israel, 19-35; and G. W. Coats, “The Joseph Story and Ancient Wisdom: A Reappraisal,” CBQ 35 (1973): 285-97. tn Heb “lie down with.” The verb שָׁכַב (shakhav) “to lie down” can be a euphemism for going to bed for sexual relations."
      ],
